commit e0d4fc6eb7c98d7f1dd5b3b9c765edb19397e682
Author: givis <givis@local>
Date:   Wed Nov 4 15:24:26 2026 +0000

    prefix-replay-depth: hash promotion must tolerate aligned publications
    
    Second engine-killing assert in the partial-hash machinery (11-04 14:58
    UTC, ~20 h after the CoW fix, [partial-cow] never fired — an independent
    path): cache_full_blocks asserted a pre-hashed new full block always
    carries a PARTIAL publication (block_hash_num_tokens < num_hash_tokens).
    An aligned landing/checkpoint publication instead registers the chain
    hash AT the full token count; when such a block re-entered the caching
    window the strict < killed the engine.
    
    Promotion now handles three cases: equal count + same hash = no-op (the
    entry under this key is already the one we would insert); strict partial
    = the original remove-and-reinsert promotion; anything else (None /
    stale) = warn with block id and counts, retract, re-register. Cache
    bookkeeping degrades, never kills.
    
    Sibling hardening: the boundary-offload loop asserted
    block.block_hash_num_tokens is not None before offering a boundary to
    the connector; a hash without a count now skips the offer instead of
    dying.

diff --git a/vllm/v1/core/block_pool.py b/vllm/v1/core/block_pool.py
